 "item", "numeric-id": 1066, "id": "Q1066"}, "type": "wikibase-entityid"}, "datatype": "wikibase-item"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q9761$B648B27A-57FF-4EF8-B8A8-1689B00D8FC7", "rank": "normal"}], "P19": [{"mainsnak": {"snaktype": "value", "property": "P19", "hash": "3cba9f1c2fd1cbb846bb90bd0e6a6a9a624755e8", "datavalue": {"value": "Shorty Sherock was a great trumpet player. He played with Horace Heidt. But Nat Pierce, I got Nat Pierce the job in the band. All right? But after that Buddy called me. And the way I joined the band, I get into town and I go to his suite and he said the first set was seven o'clock, because you played for dancing then. And I remember all the guys that were in the band I could tell you their name...", "type": "string"}, "datatype": "string"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q9761$B73EB92D-B3AC-4585-B6E9-C8E5C6362BF9", "rank": "normal"}]}}